WEBVTT

00:00:00.425 --> 00:00:08.358
In this video, you will see how many people found your contest: page visits, visits from your QR code, and votes, day by day.

00:00:08.358 --> 00:00:10.732
That tells you which kind of sharing works.

00:00:10.732 --> 00:00:11.853
We start on the map.

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:14.364
Start at SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:17.636 --> 00:00:20.186
On the home page, tap Use my location.

00:00:22.024 --> 00:00:23.004
Then tap Allow.

00:00:28.307 --> 00:00:31.515
Now look at the top of the map, beside the search box.

00:00:31.515 --> 00:00:34.297
See your picture, or your initial, in a circle?

00:00:34.297 --> 00:00:38.860
That is your account menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:39.561
Tap it.

00:00:41.883 --> 00:00:43.846
In the menu, tap Your contests.

00:00:45.593 --> 00:00:49.686
That is where the contests you run, and the homes you entered, live.

00:00:49.686 --> 00:00:50.543
Tap Mine.

00:00:52.383 --> 00:00:54.353
This is your personal page.

00:00:54.353 --> 00:00:59.825
It lists the contests you run, if you run any, and the homes you entered, with their status.

00:00:59.825 --> 00:01:01.933
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:01:03.716 --> 00:01:07.856
This opens your dashboard, the control room for your contest.

00:01:07.856 --> 00:01:09.857
Want to know whether your sharing is working?

00:01:09.857 --> 00:01:10.763
Tap Promote.

00:01:12.486 --> 00:01:21.477
Activity shows three numbers: how many people have visited your contest page, how many arrived by scanning your QR code, and how many people have voted.

00:01:22.378 --> 00:01:25.293
Below, a chart shows the votes for each day.

00:01:25.293 --> 00:01:27.866
Use it to see which sharing worked best.

00:01:27.866 --> 00:01:32.398
If votes jump the day after a flyer went up, or after an email, do more of that.

00:01:33.269 --> 00:01:35.618
Next up: Add sponsors and logos.
